{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00042",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.08,
      "end_seconds": 3.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Good afternoon. Take a seat, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.36,
      "end_seconds": 8.21,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "Hi, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.4,
      "end_seconds": 15.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.79,
      "end_seconds": 19.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "So, you came on your own today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.89,
      "end_seconds": 22.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "I mean, yes, I managed on my own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.56,
      "end_seconds": 26.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "So, how have things been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 27.47,
      "end_seconds": 30.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Well, he's been feeling very thirsty, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.82,
      "end_seconds": 36.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "When did you first notice it? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.95,
      "end_seconds": 51.06,
      "duration_seconds": 13.11,
      "text": "For nearly five years, I'd say. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.44,
      "end_seconds": 55.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.3,
      "end_seconds": 59.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "So, a four out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.94,
      "end_seconds": 63.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.58,
      "end_seconds": 69.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Right, when it starts I tend to get blurry vision as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.16,
      "end_seconds": 73.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Have you been feeling very thirsty at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.16,
      "end_seconds": 78.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "A bit, last winter. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.83,
      "end_seconds": 82.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.06,
      "end_seconds": 96.77,
      "duration_seconds": 12.71,
      "text": "Right, for the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.11,
      "end_seconds": 98.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "What about chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.48,
      "end_seconds": 102.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I mean, not at all, no chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.12,
      "end_seconds": 106.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Any abdominal pain, vomiting or foot sores?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.5,
      "end_seconds": 112.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Um, no, no abdominal pain, vomiting or foot sores."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.59,
      "end_seconds": 115.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Right, and your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.05,
      "end_seconds": 118.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.43,
      "end_seconds": 124.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Okay, do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.35,
      "end_seconds": 128.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.52,
      "end_seconds": 150.43,
      "duration_seconds": 20.91,
      "text": "Okay, high cholesterol, that's already on your record. Good to know. Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.73,
      "end_seconds": 153.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.43,
      "end_seconds": 156.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Alright, any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.2,
      "end_seconds": 160.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.32,
      "end_seconds": 166.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 167.84,
      "end_seconds": 170.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "It's rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.53,
      "end_seconds": 189.95,
      "duration_seconds": 15.42,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.33,
      "end_seconds": 194.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "So, good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.09,
      "end_seconds": 197.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.17,
      "end_seconds": 207.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.24,
      "end_seconds": 231.26,
      "duration_seconds": 13.02,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.5 degrees, respiratory rate 14. And BMI works out to 24.0, weight 77 kilos, heart rate 84, pressure 148 over 94, SpO2 98 percent on room air, height 179 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.85,
      "end_seconds": 233.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.55,
      "end_seconds": 237.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.86,
      "end_seconds": 240.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.76,
      "end_seconds": 242.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.04,
      "end_seconds": 245.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Take a breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.39,
      "end_seconds": 257.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Sensation to the monofilament is reduced on the right foot."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.17,
      "end_seconds": 286.03,
      "duration_seconds": 22.86,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. Putting it all together, I think we're dealing with diabetes that isn't well controlled at this stage. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.08,
      "end_seconds": 295.02,
      "duration_seconds": 7.94,
      "text": "Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've been feeling very thirsty for nearly five years, and no abdominal pain or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.37,
      "end_seconds": 298.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Yes, um, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.84,
      "end_seconds": 313.81,
      "duration_seconds": 14.97,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.15,
      "end_seconds": 315.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.33,
      "end_seconds": 332.94,
      "duration_seconds": 15.61,
      "text": "I'm going to order an eye check, for diabetes. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We should do kidney function tests for diabetes. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.49,
      "end_seconds": 334.48,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.93,
      "end_seconds": 342.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Let's use glimepiride, 1 milligrams, before breakfast, until we review. That should help with blood sugar control."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.68,
      "end_seconds": 345.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.76,
      "end_seconds": 358.64,
      "duration_seconds": 11.88,
      "text": "Cut back on sweets, sugary drinks and white rice, and keep to regular meal times. Check your feet every day, and never walk barefoot. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.19,
      "end_seconds": 366.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "Okay. I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you vomit repeatedly or become drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.64,
      "end_seconds": 370.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Um, yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.4,
      "end_seconds": 374.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.91,
      "end_seconds": 376.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.98,
      "end_seconds": 382.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.85,
      "text": "Right, can you run through the plan with me quickly, just to be certain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 384.35,
      "end_seconds": 391.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "So, I take the glimepiride, 1 milligrams, before breakfast and come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.71,
      "end_seconds": 398.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 399.01,
      "end_seconds": 401.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Alright, thanks. Bye for now."
    }
  ]
}